// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
// docker/igla_train: the IGLA CODER GPU training image, docker/igla-train.Dockerfile as built on
// 2026-10-31, as a t27 text with one home (Trinity-S-AI-DNA/t27#13007). The text carries the ownership
// fix: `useradd` and `chown -R appuser:appuser /workspace` run before `COPY --chown` and `USER appuser`,
// so the later `RUN echo > /workspace/validate_env.sh` writes into a directory appuser owns. Every byte
// is printable ASCII or a newline; the three identity lines read `phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3` (L3 PURITY).
//
// Why the text lives here and the Dockerfile is a build product, not a committed file:
// specs/policy/own_language.t27 counts a Dockerfile anywhere outside gen/ as hand-written foreign code
// (313 lines against a cap of 40 per file), and specs/policy/l2_generation.t27 accepts a tracked file
// under gen/ only when a t27c backend (c, verilog, rust, zig, json) reproduces it byte for byte, which a
// t27b-written text is not. So no copy is committed; the bytes are emitted on demand. Why t27b writes
// them: t27c has no subcommand that writes a spec's str constant to a file, so
// specs/docker/igla_train_main.t27 follows specs/t27os/plist_main.t27 and writes `dockerfile()` through
// the `write` import of specs/t27os/pty_sys.t27. The recipe, from the repository root, as run 2026-10-31:
//   t27b build specs/docker/igla_train_main.t27 -o dm.o --macho
//   ld -lSystem -syslibroot $(xcrun --show-sdk-path) -e _main -o dm dm.o
//   ./dm > gen/docker/igla-train.Dockerfile
// `t27c test-report specs/docker/igla_train.t27` runs the tests below, and the same command on the main
// spec runs its one test (the @extern import is linked by t27b and never called from a test). A Makefile
// target and a CI drift step would both be hand-written foreign lines, so neither is added; the emitted
// file is compared against the ASCII source with `cmp` by hand (10724 bytes, exit 0 on 2026-10-31).
//
// Pieces follow the Dockerfile's own sections, in order. Each is a counted string: the _LEN rides along
// because gen-c lowers str to a pointer without .len, and a test checks that every piece ends with its
// newline exactly where its _LEN says. A change to the text moves DOCKERFILE_LEN in the same commit.
module DockerIglaTrain;
use claw::text;

pub const D_HEAD : str = "# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n# Dockerfile for IGLA CODER GPU Training\n# Based on AMD ROCm 6.2 for CMP 170H (RDNA3)\n# phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY\n\n# Use Ubuntu 22.04 LTS as base\nFROM ubuntu:22.04\n\n";
